## Locating Desktop CLI & Version Check

Requires a local EditHere installation or extracted portable package (never install packages silently or mutate global PATH). Resolve `edithere-cli` in order and verify `--version` + `--help` (confirm `image-set` support):

1. User-provided path in the current turn, or `references/local-installation.md` if present;
2. `$env:EDITHERE_CLI`, `PATH`, or default install location (Windows: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\EditHere\edithere-cli.exe`; macOS: `/Applications/EditHere.app/Contents/MacOS/edithere-cli` or `~/Applications/...`).

```powershell
& $EditHereCli --version
& $EditHereCli --help
```

If missing or below required version, direct the user to <https://github.com/Inginnng/EditHere/releases/latest> rather than switching to an older binary.

## Commands & Session Execution

```text
edithere-cli status
edithere-cli open <image-video-or-manifest>
edithere-cli capture
edithere-cli export <image-video-project-or-feedback> --output <new-feedback.json> [--embed-image | --no-image] [--preview]
edithere-cli annotate <image-video-project-or-manifest> --output <new-feedback.json> [--page-context "Page label"] [--embed-image | --no-image] [--preview] [--timeout 1800]
```

- **Unique `--output`**: Must be an absolute path that does NOT exist yet inside an existing parent directory (e.g., `.edithere/reviews/`).
- **Single-process wait**: `open` and `capture` return immediately and do not replace `annotate`. Wait for `annotate` to exit `0` with stdout `ok: true` and a valid output JSON before editing code.
- **Sandboxes & recovery**: `status` / `open` / `capture` / `annotate` need logged-in desktop access (exit code `8` on restricted sandboxes -> use approved escalation such as `require_escalated`). See [Exit Codes, Version Baselines & Troubleshooting](references/troubleshooting.md).
